SUMMARY:Friday Nights at OMCA with Kiyomi & Cal Raijin Taiko
LOCATION:Oakland Museum\, 1000 Oak St\, Oakland\, CA 94607
DESCRIPTION:Live Performance by Cal Raijin Taiko\, Live Music by Kiyomi\, M
 usic Set by DJ Dailo Mac\, Live Figure Drawing with Sketchboard Co.\, Annu
 al Fall Teacher Night\, ScholarMatch\, and Gallery Chats Celebrate the ope
 ning week of BeHere/1942: A New Lens on the Japanese American Incarceratio
 n this Friday Night at OMCA with an evening of music\, culture\, and commu
 nity. The Garden Stage features two dynamic performances\, beginning with 
 Cal Raijin Taiko\, whose original compositions blend the tradition of Japa
 nese taiko drumming with contemporary influences. Following\, Bay Area sin
 ger-songwriter Kiyomi brings her soulful alternative R&B sound to the stag
 e\, weaving rich harmonies\, live looping\, and heartfelt storytelling int
 o an intimate performance that invites audiences to slow down and connect.
 \nhttps://museumca.org/event/friday-nights-at-omca-with-kiyomi-cal-raijin-
 taiko/\nFrom Pushpin Bay Area: https://pushpin.city/bayarea/
URL:https://museumca.org/event/friday-nights-at-omca-with-kiyomi-cal-raijin
 -taiko/
END:VEVENT
